# Coding Standards

## Immutability (CRITICAL)

ALWAYS create new objects, NEVER mutate existing ones.

```
// DO: spread operator で新しいオブジェクトを作成
const updated = { ...user, name: 'New' }

// DON'T: 直接変更
user.name = 'New'  // ← 禁止
```

言語を問わず、変更が必要な場合は新しいインスタンスを生成すること。

## File Organization

- MANY SMALL FILES > FEW LARGE FILES
- 200-400 lines typical, **800 lines max**
- High cohesion, low coupling
- Organize by feature/domain, not by type

## Functions

- **50 lines max** per function
- No deep nesting (>4 levels)
- Single responsibility

## Error Handling

ALWAYS handle errors using the language's idiomatic pattern.
Never swallow errors silently. Always include context in error messages.

```
// DO
return fmt.Errorf("failed to fetch user %d: %w", id, err)

// DON'T
catch (e) {} // ← 禁止: エラーの握り潰し
```

## Input Validation

ALWAYS validate user input at system boundaries using the project's validation library.
Internal function calls between trusted code do not need redundant validation.

## Code Quality Checklist

Before marking work complete:
- [ ] Readable, well-named code
- [ ] Functions < 50 lines, files < 800 lines
- [ ] No deep nesting (>4 levels)
- [ ] Proper error handling (no silent catches)
- [ ] No debug logging left in
- [ ] No hardcoded values
- [ ] Immutable patterns used
